Dear all,

On June 16-17th, the library and the postdoc union are hosting a Software Carpentry <http://software-carpentry.org/> Bootcamp. Software Carpentry’s aim is to teach researchers basic computing concepts and skills so that they can get more done in less time, and with less pain. The curriculum will be:
Introduction to Unix shell
Version control & an introduction to databases and SQL
Introduction to programming with R
Testing your code and creating reproducible analyses

I HIGHLY recommend their curriculum even if you have some R experience, as it teaches you not just to do statistical analyses in R but the tools to manage data and make those analyses automated and reproducible.

There is a registration fee of $37.92. D-RUG can support up to 8 of our members attending. The first 8 D-RUG listserv members to send me their registration confirmations will be reimbursed after the workshop.

Space is limited, so register ASAP! More details at the registration link below:

 <http://ucdavis-swc.eventbrite.com>http://ucdavis-swc.eventbrite.com

Questions? See the FAQ <http://software-carpentry.org/faq.html#bootcamps>, or contact the organizers: Jonathan Cachat (jca...@ucdavis.edu; @jcachat <https://twitter.com/jcachat>) and Benjamin Schwessinger (bschwe...@ucdavis.edu; @schwessinger <https://twitter.com/schwessinger>).

Thanks to UC Library <http://www.lib.ucdavis.edu/c> and the Union for Postdocs <http://uaw5810.org/> for organizing this bootcamp.

Best,

Noam

