I second Kristina's link to QuickR.  Best site ever!  I still use it for reference.  Another reference I use all the time is the book Applied Spatial Data Analysis with R (Bivand, Pebesma, and Gomez-Rubio)... it's on my table right now... and Plant's spatial stats book.  I know the library has electronic access to the first one.  In general, I find the help usually quite helpful as well as the vignettes - that's how I started with the Vegan and Raster packages.

best,
Michele

