Hi all,

Our last D-RUG session of the quarter will be this Monday, 3:10-5PM in WIckson 2124. In the first half of the session, Kristina Wolf will be presenting an analysis for feedback. From Kristina:
>
> I will be presenting on my project in which I manipulated timing/amount/frequency of summer watering to flush out weeds in a restored perennial grassland. I am hoping for some feedback on my stats analysis for non-parametric data (non-normal and unequal variances); I used Friedman and Kruskal-Wallis test. I also did post-hoc multiple comparisons but I don’t trust the results for that because the LSDs don’t look right. I have tried negative binomial, beta regression, various transformations, etc., that didn’t seem to work and/or fit the data well.

Look out later today for a survey to decide summer D-RUG meeting times.

Best,

Noam
